# Citation File Format 1.2.0. https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# There is deliberately no .zenodo.json beside this file. Zenodo reads both, and where both are
# present only .zenodo.json is used and this file is ignored entirely
# (https://help.zenodo.org/docs/github/describe-software/).
#
# `doi` and `date-released` are absent on purpose. Both are known only once a GitHub Release has
# been archived by Zenodo, and a placeholder in either would be an invalid value rather than a
# missing one. Add the VERSION doi, not the concept doi: a verdict is the output of one rule set, so
# a citation that does not name the version has not said which instrument produced its numbers.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite the specific version you ran."
type: software
title: langaccess
abstract: >-
  langaccess audits the language accessibility of a website. The tool renders the site in a
  headless browser and classifies, for each language present, the access provided: English-only
  content, a machine-translation widget, or text authored by the site itself. Each classification
  is returned with its supporting evidence, the URL and quoted text that decided it, and the
  numbered classification rules that were applied.
authors:
  - family-names: Yoo
    given-names: Nari
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8467-7048"
    email: nariyoo@umich.edu
    affiliation: University of Michigan School of Social Work
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nariyoo/langaccess"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-SA-3.0
keywords:
  - language access
  - multilingual
  - website audit
  - machine translation
  - limited English proficiency
  - health equity
  - web measurement
